      "statusChangeNewStatus": "tracked",
      "value": "Your U# code and your Graph do two different things.\nIn your U# code, I would expect the \"NoiseMaker\" to be set to active in Start, which I assume will play a sound. Later, when the gameObject with CollisionTestBox on it hits a collider, it will Destroy itself, leaving the NoiseMaker to play the sound.\nIn your Udon Graph, I would expect the NoiseMaker to be set to active in Start. Later, when the gameObject with this Graph on it hits a collider, it will Set the gameObject stored as the \"Self\" variable to Inactive.\nI ran a simple graph test that logs the Collision when OnCollisionEnter is called (graphic attached). This program is attached to a simple box with a BoxCollider and a Rigidbody and placed above a Plane with a MeshCollider. When I run the scene, the box falls and logs \"UnityEngine.Collision\" to my console as expected.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
